  "summary": "Malicious code in bigops-tinkoff-telephony-mock (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package loads a bundled downloader (_runtime.js) that fetches a platform-specific binary payload over HTTPS from Cloudflare Workers hosts oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, and oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev (paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, /pkg/package.exe), with a fallback DNS-TXT channel via c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru (and ext[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, pkg[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru). The downloaded binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (or dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe in the temp dir on Windows), made executable, and launched detached in the background via /bin/sh -c '\u003cpath\u003e \u0026' or cmd.exe /c start /b. A stamp file at /tmp/.analytics_state throttles re-execution. This is remote binary download-and-execute at package load time.",
